/E (Every generation produces its own entrepreneurs. For Gen Z, entrepreneurship looks like reselling thrifted clothing on Depop, tutoring classmates for cash, freelancing on Fiverr, and building audiences on TikTok. The hustle is already there. What's missing is the bridge between what students already do and what they could build.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (In a survey of 58 college students, 66% said they had never considered starting a business. But within that same group, students reported tutoring, freelancing, reselling, and creating content for money. They're already entrepreneurs. They just don't call it that, and they certainly don't think Shopify or other similar platforms are for them. Only 53% associated Shopify with opening a store, placing it behind Etsy and Instagram in student awareness. Recognized, but not understood.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
