370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Of every feature we tested, the duplicate functionality generated the strongest response. The premise is straightforward: find a student store, click duplicate, and Sidekick generates a copy of the layout, theme configuration, and recommended app stack. The student starts from a proven structure rather than a blank page.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (This directly addresses the most common barrier in our research. 33% of survey respondents said their biggest obstacle was coming up with a good idea. The clone feature reframes that problem entirely: instead of generating an idea from nothing, students see what others have built and begin from there. One participant captured the logic precisely: )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E <8D596F752063616E2074616B65207768617420776F726B732C207768617427732070726F76656E20746F20776F726B2C20616E642075736520697420696E20796F757220636173652E20496620697420776F726B7320666F72207468656D2C20697420776F726B7320666F7220796F752E8E20>
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (The duplication is designed with intellectual property protection built in. It transfers structure only; not branding, product photography, copy, or customer data. Additionally, every cloned store includes attribution to the original founder. This means getting cloned becomes a form of credibility for the original creator, not a risk. The same model has proven effective across platforms like Figma Community and Framer, where shared templates drive adoption without compromising the original creator.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Our prototype validated the concept through the duplicate entry point and store detail view, but did not extend into the full AI-assisted duplication flow. Simulating functional store generation with realistic data exceeded the scope of a ten-week course. The user testing responses suggest the concept is strong enough to warrant dedicated prototyping of the technical execution as a next phase.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
