<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 202 0 R
/T (So what can Shopify actually do with this?)
/E (So what can Shopify actually do with this?)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (First, build the Student Showcase. Our prototype testing showed that 78% of students found student-built stores believable and trustworthy, and 66% responded positively to founder stories specifically. Examples from real students will close the gap between awareness and action.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (1)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (Second, lead with free. Of every feature and value proposition we tested, "free until your first sale" was the single most compelling element for 45% of participants. It needs to be the first thing a student sees, not something they find after scrolling.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (2)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (Third, fix discoverability. 44% of users never found pricing without being prompted. The content is good, but students just can't find it. Information architecture is as important as the message itself.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (3)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (Fourth, make the clone feature impossible to miss. Students who got it were immediately excited, while the others just scrolled past. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (4)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (Shopify already has 80% brand awareness among Gen Z, but only 7.3% of its merchant base is between 18 and 24. That is just how much room there is left to grow. The students are already there. The platform just needs to make it obvious that the door is open.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
